    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0104" n="92" xml:id="pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.48/119: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-09T17:00:00+02:00">January 9, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 9—3:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. Department’s telegram 10, January 6, 6 [<hi rendition="#italic">8</hi>] p.m.
                    Marshal Petain<anchor n="5" xml:id="d78-f1"/> and Foreign Minister Flandin
                    assure me this afternoon that the conditions governing the shipment of relief
                    goods are acceptable to the French Government.</p>
                <p>I shall telegraph in detail tomorrow concerning the interview.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leahy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d78-f1" n="5" xml:id="d78-f1-content">
                <p>Marshal Henri Philippe Pétain, French Chief of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
